From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dave Stevenson <dave.stevenson@raspberrypi.com>
Date: Wed, 7 May 2025 18:10:25 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] v4l2codecs: Update bit_size and data_byte_offset based on
 updated docs

From discussion whilst upstreaming the Raspberry Pi HEVC decoder,
the bit_size and data_byte_offset definitions have been clarified.
They haven't been used by drivers until now.

Update the usage to match the new documentation.

Link: https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/gstreamer/gstreamer/-/merge_requests/9247
---
 sys/v4l2codecs/gstv4l2codech265dec.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/sys/v4l2codecs/gstv4l2codech265dec.c
+++ b/sys/v4l2codecs/gstv4l2codech265dec.c
@@ -793,8 +793,8 @@ gst_v4l2_codec_h265_dec_fill_slice_param
   /* *INDENT-OFF* */
   params = &g_array_index (self->slice_params, struct v4l2_ctrl_hevc_slice_params, n);
   *params = (struct v4l2_ctrl_hevc_slice_params) {
-    .bit_size = (slice_size + sc_offset) * 8,
-    .data_byte_offset = get_slice_header_byte_offset (slice) + sc_offset,
+    .bit_size = (slice_size - get_slice_header_byte_offset(slice)) * 8,
+    .data_byte_offset = get_slice_header_byte_offset (slice) + sc_offset + self->bitstream_map.size,
     .num_entry_point_offsets = slice_hdr->num_entry_point_offsets,
     .nal_unit_type = slice->nalu.type,
     .nuh_temporal_id_plus1 = slice->nalu.temporal_id_plus1,
